      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To investigate whether a relationship exists between personality and expression of pain in women with endometriosis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "STUDY DESIGN",
          "content": "With use of the Rosenzweig picture frustration study, the personality of women with endometriosis was assessed. These results were then correlated with the manifestation of pain."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Women without dysmenorrhea tended to be less assertive compared with women who complained of dysmenorrhea and women without endometriosis. Those women without dysmenorrhea showed a destructive attitude in face of a problem."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Personality affected the expression of pain. Pain caused by endometriosis was influenced by each personality type."
        }
      ]},
